menu "LCD UI"

    config MINIHUB_LCD_UI
        bool "Enable LCD UI (esp-brookesia JSON UI)"
        depends on !MINIHUB_NET_ETH
        default n
        help
            Mutually exclusive with Ethernet on some boards (EMAC vs RGB LCD).

    config MINIHUB_LCD_UI_REFRESH_MS
        int "LCD UI fallback resync period (ms)"
        depends on MINIHUB_LCD_UI
        default 30000
        range 500 300000
        help
            Point updates reach the screen through the Hub event bus, so this is
            not the refresh interval. It is how often the panel re-reads every
            point in case an event was dropped: a subscription that silently
            misses one update sticks, because a display has no reconnect. Set it
            high (the default is 30 s); the coalesce window that actually gates
            redraws is fixed at 100 ms in the firmware.

    config MINIHUB_LCD_UI_VERSION
        string "LCD UI bundle version"
        depends on MINIHUB_LCD_UI
        default MINIHUB_VERSION
        help
            Version stamped into /data/ui/version.txt and published under
            LCD_UI/v<ver>/ for GET /api/ui. Independent of firmware and web so a
            panel-only fix can ship without bumping either. Defaults to the
            product MINIHUB_VERSION.

endmenu
